# FABLE-SONNET-UNIT-FIELD-WRITE-20260923-129 (Opus's -128 side finding). A
# method assigning a unit field declared ABOVE it used to fail translation
# SILENTLY ("translation failed with no located diagnostic"): l2_check_body
# already accepted the statement (l2_own_unit_seen, backward visibility for
# every non-callable, author 2026-09-22 blog 857692c), but l2_emit_body's
# own-field lookup for an assignment TARGET (l2_own_find_last) lacked the
# same unit-field fallback its sibling l2_own_find already had, so the name
# fell all the way through to a dead silent return: 1. `x: 7` inside bump is
# an ordinary assignment to the unit's own field x through the lexical
# parent -- the same route node\x already takes (author Q9): "any assignment
# projects into the field of the structure that owns it."
#
# Three shapes: write from a method, read back at unit level (the reported
# repro); write then read within the same method, same activation; write
# from inside a nested if body within the method (the write route does not
# care which control-flow depth it runs at, only which method -- mi is
# unchanged by if/while nesting).
int: x 5
int: y 5

fn: bump () int
    x: 7
    return: 0
end: bump

fn: bump_and_read () int
    y: 8
    if: y != 8
        return: 1
    return: 0
end: bump_and_read

int: z 5
fn: bump_nested () int
    if: 1 != 0
        z: 9
    return: 0
end: bump_nested

int: r
bump()
if: x != 7
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 90; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
r: bump_and_read()
if: r != 0
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 91; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
bump_nested()
if: z != 9
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 92; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 0; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
